strange end of the season for miami  dolphins just a couple of years removed  from a playoff berth adam gase is fired  mike tannenbaum is out chris greer stays  as the gm and essentially is in charge  of the football operations hires brian  flores to be the head coach the  expectations are incredibly low and i'd  always prefer shireen low expectations  to high expectations it's a lot easier  to clear that low bar than it is to to  meet when everyone expects you to be a  playoff team and make some noise in  january so i kind of like where the  dolphins are because they're in kind of  a no-lose situation the the question is  how much better can they really be in  one off season with what chris greer and  brian flores are trying to do starting  with trying to find a quarterback a  franchise quarterback for the first time  since dan marino retired 20 years ago  well you know my husband's an orioles  fan and a dolphins fan so i joke about  he needs to find the losingest teams in  basketball and hockey and pick those up  too and  early in the off season i said you know  you're going to have the worst team in  the nfl i no longer believe that i think  this is a mediocre football team i think  it's going to be a little bit better  than people expect however having said  that i don't think they're going to have  a better record than they had last  season i'm just saying i think they're  going to be better than what people  expect them to be which is the worst  team or one of the worst teams in the  nfl and i actually like them at the  quarterback position i love what they've  done in the off season at the  quarterback position they're way better  off than than many maybe most teams in  the nfl at the quarterback position with  the veteran and a guy you expect to be  your franchise guy  yeah and and look  i  so many people expect them to be  absolutely dreadful and they haven't  been absolutely dreadful in a long time  they've been competitive but not  competitive enough we've got one playoff  birth in the last decade uh they haven't  had any success in the postseason but  you know they're trying to build  something now and there's this tension i  think at the top of the organization  between the burning desire to win that  chris greer and brian flores definitely  have i i just wonder how much ownership  really buys into the idea of continuing  this 79 8 and 8 hope to get lucky get to  the playoffs because there really is an  argument to be made that if you take  your lumps  heavily one year and you have that three  and thirteen bottom out and you put  yourself in position to go get your  franchise quarterback  that that that has you set for the next  decade and the question is did they find  their franchise quarterback without  having to bottom out can josh rosen  become the guy who who finally bridges  that gap back to dan moreno because it's  been a long revolving door of not great  quarterbacks for the dolphins since  mourinho retired have we seen enough  from josh rosen have any confidence that  he can come in and be a guy that that we  say wow boy the cardinals really got  that wrong by getting rid of josh rosen  i don't think we've seen it yet but he  was the 10th overall pick for a reason  and i do think he can be that guy and  you know what if he is that guy we're  all gonna say oh my gosh the dolphins  are geniuses what if this guy turns out  to be better than kyler murray and he  could be and if he is then i think the  miami dolphins have hit on this without  having to use that high pick as you said  to get their franchise guy instead the  cardinals used it and they got him  basically for free this is a very low  risk proposition for the miami dolphins  and  the problem to me that they face is to  find out if josh rosen is that guy  they're going to have to play him this  season at some point to find out if he  is that guy otherwise if they're that  bad as you said they've got to go out  and draft a quarterback next year and  that'll be their franchise guys so it  all depends on how ryan fitzpatrick is  going to keep his job as long as this  team can can win football games  initially and if they lose enough games  you've got to get josh rosen in there  and get him in there quickly  i think you need to give rosen every  opportunity to prove he's the right guy  as of week one i mean i i think that if  rosen is gonna become a franchise  quarterback and if he is worthy of being  the 10th overall pick in the draft if he  is worthy of the second round pick the  dolphins sent to arizona to get him even  though they played the board very well  they traded down uh  in the deeper part of round two picked  up an extra second round pick from the  saints by doing that and then sent that  lower second round pick to arizona for  all those things rosen should be better  than ryan fitzpatrick and he should be  able to be the week one starter if he's  not that's alarming but uh you know at  some point you're right they have to  evaluate him this year and they have to  see what they have because they may have  a decision to make next year but they  have him for three years at 6.3 million  total that is peanuts as far as  quarterbacks go the cardinals ended up  paying him over 11 million dollars for  one year so the the dolphins have worked  this well the question becomes how does  it work out from here and as it relates  to the dolphins draft shireen i love the  fact that they got christian wilkins at  13. that there's something about that  there's just an energy you know he came  out and he slammed into roger goodell he  did the jump slam into roger goodell  he's got a great personality now i know  that doesn't make for a great football  player but there's just you know the  dolphins need  someone that gets people excited if it's  not going to be the quarterback and it  hasn't been for a long time it's got to  be another player and i think christian  wilkins is going to be a guy who really  energizes dolphins fans and makes them  feel good again about following a team  that has been mediocre at best for two  decades  i absolutely love that draft pick and  this is a football team that's pretty  good on the back end  maybe really good on the back end and if  they can get that pass rush now i know  they've lost  cameron wake but christian wilkins is  going to be a star in this league i have  no doubts about that i think this was a  great pick  by the miami dolphins  and he improves their defense and  improves their defense right away and  bryant flores is going to improve their  defense too just from a coaching aspect  i think he was a great hire possibly the  best hire in this cycle of coaches  and i do think the dolphins will  eventually win it's not going to be this  year but i do think the dolphins will  take some sort of step this season maybe  not record wise but i think they'll take  a step  and be a better football team overall  even if the record doesn't say that  they're a better football team  we're all constantly evaluating which of  the other teams in the afc east will be  ready to compete to fill the vacuum  whenever the patriots fall off that  assumes the patriots ever do  fall off i'm not ready to admit that  they're ever going to fall off but the  bills in the jets most people would say  are best positioned for now but yeah the  dolphins are just a seasonal way of  exceeding expectations to get us to say  this may be a team that we have to take  seriously again and and i remember you  know sharing when we were growing up the  dolphins were and even though they were  aqua right they were an intimidating  team they were a good team when the  dolphins showed up you were probably  going to lose that day it's been a long  time since that vibe has been around  yeah it certainly has i went to a  thanksgiving day game when the dolphins  played the cowboys and they were that  intimidating team and that team that  everybody wanted to see they had those  personalities that you're talking about  well it wasn't it wasn't the leonlette  game was it  no no this is back in the 70s  yeah oh that they weren't as  intimidating then but they ended up  thanks to leonlette coming out of it  with a victory we got one hour down one  more to go we'll be right back with more  right after this  [Music]  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports

